The Motto

I think this captures it succinctly:

A signature proves identity.

A bootloader initializes capability.

A lithographic signature bootloader does both.

That also circles back to your earlier distinction between copy and carry. The tattoo doesn’t copy the system onto skin; it carries enough invariant structure to reliably regenerate the intended system when combined with the appropriate interpreter. In that sense, it’s less like a storage device and more like a seed crystal or a BIOS: compact, stable, and designed to bootstrap something much larger.